## Chapter Field Requirements
- The `chapters` array must contain exactly {{ batch_end - batch_start + 1 }} entries, with `chapter_number` ranging consecutively from {{ batch_start }} to {{ batch_end }}.
- Each chapter object must explicitly contain a `title` field; the title can be short but cannot be omitted; cannot use only `goal`, `beats_summary`, or `main_plot_points` as a substitute for the title.
- Each chapter object must start with three fields: `chapter_number`, `title`, `goal`, then write array fields like `beats_summary`, `main_plot_points`.
- Each chapter must include: chapter number, title, narrative goal, beats summary, main plot points, subplot points, subplot focus, element focus, POV ID/display name, POV switch or not, main setting, expected word count, involved character IDs/display names, cast_plan, emotional_plan, scene_design_goals, notes, chapter-end hook, and micro-payoffs.
- Field names must use: `chapter_number`, `title`, `goal`, `beats_summary`, `main_plot_points`, `subplot_points`, `subplot_focus`, `element_focus`, `pov_character_id`, `pov_character_name`, `pov_character`, `pov_switch`, `setting`, `expected_word_count`, `involved_character_ids`, `required_character_ids`, `support_character_ids`, `involved_character_names`, `involved_characters`, `cast_plan`, `emotional_plan`, `scene_design_goals`, `notes`, `expected_hook`, `expected_payoffs`; aliases like `pov`, `main_scenes`, `target_word_count` are forbidden.
{% if design_matrix %}- All `*_character_ids` and `cast_plan.*_ids` can only use the entity_id from the chapter design matrix; display name fields must be filled back according to the Entity Catalog.
{% elif character_whitelist %}- `pov_character` and `involved_characters` can only use the formal names from the whitelist above; `involved_characters` lists the whitelisted characters involved in this chapter, including the POV character; list only names, no descriptions.
{% else %}- `involved_characters` must list all characters appearing in this chapter, including the POV character; list only names, no descriptions.
{% endif %}
- `emotional_plan` must include `subject_entity_id`, `entry_state`, `pressure_source`, `relationship_choice`, `turning_emotion`, `exit_aftertaste`, `expression_channels`; must not be written as abstract theme slogans.
- `scene_design_goals` must list 2-5 goals that subsequent PLAN_CHAPTER can implement as scenes, which must come from plot_duties / emotional_plan / hook_payoff_duties.
- `main_plot_points` length {{ main_min }}-{{ main_max }}; `beats_summary` length {{ beats_min }}-{{ beats_max }}; `subplot_points` length 0-{{ subplot_max }}.
- `element_focus` must be an array, with elements only allowed from the `element_id` of the candidate expansion elements from earlier, length 0-{{ element_focus_max }}.
- `beats_summary` array elements must be pure plot sentences, forbidden with tags or "Beat n:" prefixes, forbidden to expand into scene outlines.
- `expected_hook` and `expected_payoffs` must exist in every chapter and must belong to the same chapter object.
- `expected_hook` contains hook_type, hook_strength, hook_description; `expected_payoffs` length {{ payoff_min }}-{{ payoff_max }}, each item contains payoff_type and description.
- `payoff_type` can only use: information, relationship, ability, resource, recognition, emotion, clue.
